<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Publius Canidius Crassus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/30-bce">30 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Publius Canidius <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcus-licinius-crassus">Crassus</a> was a Roman general and partisan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Mark Antony</a>, suffect consul in 40 BCE. In 36 BCE he campaigned in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberians">Iberians</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albanians">Albanians</a>, forcing them into alliance before Antony's Parthian expedition. He commanded Antony's land army at the time of Actium in 31 BCE and was executed on Octavian's orders in 30 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/publius-canidius-crassus.jpg" alt="Publius Canidius Crassus" width="320" height="224" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ancient Ptolemaic-period scribe(s) as well as Cleopatra VII of Egypt who offered her signature on the document · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Papyrus_document_containing_signature_of_Cleopatra_VII_of_Egypt.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
